# What must never reach an image. Data must be bind-mounted at runtime, not
# copied in at build time, or every container recreate would start from a
# blank or stale DB — and secrets baked into a layer go wherever the image goes.
#
# Every pattern is anchored with **/ on purpose. .dockerignore patterns match
# from the context root only: a bare `*.env` excludes ./x.env and nothing
# deeper. This file used to say `*.env`, so ATProto/pds/pds.env — the PDS's
# PLC rotation key — was copied into any image built on the node by
# `COPY ATProto ./ATProto`. `.venv/` and `__pycache__/` had the same gap.
**/data/
**/*.db
**/*.db-*
**/*.sqlite
**/*.sqlite-*
**/logs/
**/*.log

**/.venv/
**/venv/
**/env/
**/__pycache__/
**/*.py[cod]

**/.env
**/.env.*
!.env.example
**/*.env
pds-data/
cloudflared/
**/.cloudflared/

.git/
.github/

**/.DS_Store
.vscode/
.idea/
